    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēlos</span></b> , i, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μῆλος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island in the Ægean Sea, one
				of the Cyclades</i>, now <i>Milo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 23, § 70</span></i>; Paul.
			ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 124</span></i>
			Müll.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēlĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of Melos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Diagoras Melius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēlĭnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, v. 4. Melinus.</div>
